    <string name="setup_welcome_title">A Dynamic Island for your Android</string>
    <string name="setup_welcome_body">A pill around your camera that shows music, calls, timers, charging, earbuds and the notifications you choose. Tap it for more, hold it for quick controls.</string>
    <string name="setup_welcome_free_title">Free, for good</string>
    <string name="setup_welcome_free_detail">No ads, no subscriptions, no accounts</string>
    <string name="setup_welcome_open_source_detail">GPL-3.0, on GitHub</string>
    <string name="setup_welcome_no_internet_title">No internet</string>
    <string name="setup_welcome_no_internet_detail">Lagoon has no network permission. Nothing can leave your phone.</string>
    <string name="setup_overlay_title">Let it float over other apps</string>
    <string name="setup_overlay_body">The island is a small window that sits above whatever you are doing. Android calls this \"Display over other apps\" and asks you to switch it on by hand.</string>
    <string name="setup_overlay_pending">Switch it on, then come back</string>
    <string name="setup_notifications_body">This is how Lagoon knows what is playing, who is calling and what your apps want to tell you. Here is exactly what that means.</string>
    <string name="setup_notifications_disclosure">What Lagoon does with it</string>
    <string name="setup_notifications_reads_title">Reads</string>
    <string name="setup_notifications_reads_body">The title, text, icon and buttons of notifications from the apps you pick, media playback state and album art, and the dialer\'s call notification.</string>
    <string name="setup_notifications_keeps_title">Keeps</string>
    <string name="setup_notifications_keeps_body">Nothing. Content stays in memory while it is on the island and is dropped afterwards. There is no log and no database of your notifications.</string>
    <string name="setup_notifications_sends_title">Sends</string>
    <string name="setup_notifications_sends_body">Nothing. Lagoon has no internet permission, so it cannot upload anything, ever.</string>
    <string name="setup_sideload_title">Installed from outside a store?</string>
    <string name="setup_sideload_intro">Android 13 and newer grey out this setting for apps installed by hand until you allow it:</string>
    <string name="setup_sideload_step1">1. Open the setting below and try to switch Lagoon on. If it says \"restricted\", come back.</string>
    <string name="setup_sideload_step2">2. Open App info, tap the ⋮ menu, choose \"Allow restricted settings\".</string>
    <string name="setup_sideload_step3">3. Open the setting again. It will switch on now.</string>
    <string name="setup_notifications_pending">Grant it, then come back</string>
    <string name="setup_keepalive_title">Keep it running</string>
    <string name="setup_keepalive_body_stock">Stock Android keeps Lagoon\'s service alive on its own. If the island ever disappears, the Health screen shows what happened and how to fix it.</string>
    <string name="setup_keepalive_body_oem">%1$s phones close background apps that are not allowed by hand, and the island goes with them. Two minutes now saves a lot of wondering later.</string>
    <string name="setup_keepalive_note">Lagoon does not ask to be excluded from battery optimisation here. That option appears on the Health screen only if the service is actually stopped.</string>
    <string name="setup_calibrate_title">Wrap the camera</string>
    <string name="setup_calibrate_body">Lagoon read your screen\'s cutout. Fine-tune it so the ring sits evenly; the real island at the top of the screen moves as you drag.</string>
    <string name="setup_done_title_ready">You\'re set</string>
    <string name="setup_done_title_almost">Almost there</string>
    <string name="setup_done_body_ready">The island is live. Everything below can be changed later from the Home screen.</string>
    <string name="setup_done_body_almost">The island needs the two permissions above before it can show. Home keeps this checklist until it is done.</string>
    <string name="setup_home_enhanced_hint_title">Tap right at the camera</string>
    <string name="setup_home_enhanced_hint_detail">Turn on Enhanced mode so the whole island responds, including the part over the status bar.</string>
